      {
        "id": 142688,
        "name": "Donner",
        "username": "Donner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-19T18:36:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jajd2c\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/a88e4f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jajd2c:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In my opinion, VI was the best Final Fantasy, followed very closely by the original Final Fantasy Tactics and Chrono Trigger. I haven't played IV all the way through (slacking, I know), but it seems like it is nearly in that tier. VII is not. It is a good game, and one I enjoyed greatly, but not even remotely the best of the series.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I also like FFVI, Tactics, and ChronoTrigger more. &nbsp;For some reason the wobbly Cloud scenes bother me and I don't like them (when he's in the wheelchair).</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:19:58.586Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
