      {
        "id": 142689,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-19T19:05:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I like IV the best, I also love V, and XII is fantastic too.</p><p>FF VII had some great characters, the strength of the game was the team, you felt their personalities, and you liked them. &nbsp;The plot wasn't amazing, but the characters for the most part were.</p><p>Then you have the sidequests. &nbsp;They really made the game, so much to do, so many ways to delay the story and just have fun with your team.</p><p>My point is that the new game won't improve the good things, and will likely have to alter them to keep them relevant with new graphics. &nbsp;I honestly think this game being remade will take away from its appeal more than give new players access to the great game it was.</p><p>Think of the saucer games<span>, are they going to leave that all the same gameplay with better graphics? &nbsp;I can't imagine that.</span></p><p>The best parts of the game can't be improved, the cutscenes can, but at that point why not make a series instead of the game.</p><p>I think the remake will not displace the original, no matter how they dress it up.</p>",
