      {
        "id": 142693,
        "name": "Nielzabub",
        "username": "Nielzabub",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nielzabub/{size}/1986_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-20T04:48:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Think of the saucer games, are they going to leave that all the same gameplay with better graphics? &nbsp;I can't imagine that.The best parts of the game can't be improved, the cutscenes can, but at that point why not make a series instead of the game.I think the remake will not displace the original, no matter how they dress it up.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't think the remake will be better than the original, but I still think it's worth doing. As for the saucer games, I would actually really love it if they kept the bike game from the original and justified it as being retro. You could probably do the same with the other games. That might be neat.</p>",
